[agent] ## Done — full FTI pipeline built on the platform (BigQuery + Vertex AI, via `gcloud ai` / `bq`)
[agent] **Interface confirmed:** CLI mode — `gcloud {ai,auth,config,components,storage,monitoring}` + `bq`. All work ran platform-side (BigQuery SQL + BigQuery ML + Vertex AI Model Registry); nothing computed locally.
[agent] ### Pipeline (all in dataset `mlpab_mlpab08f695`)
[agent] 1. **Feature engineering → `cctxn76ccb2`** (feature group). Loaded both CSVs into BigQuery, built a combined timeline so temporal features are consistent across the train/score boundary, and engineered per-transaction fraud signals: `log_amt`, `hour`, `dow`, `is_night`, haversine `geo_dist_km` from the card's usual location, `amt_over_avg`, `amt_z`, `velocity_1h`, `velocity_24h`, `secs_since_prev`, `card_txn_cnt`, plus `amount`/`category`.
[agent] 2. **Training dataset → `cctd76ccb2`** assembled from the feature group (features + `is_fraud`).
[agent] 3. **Model → `ccmodel76ccb2`** — BigQuery ML `BOOSTED_TREE_CLASSIFIER` with `auto_class_weights` (2% base rate) and auto held-out split. **Registered to Vertex AI Model Registry** as `mlpab08f695_ccmodel76ccb2` (version 1, prefix applied). Evaluation metrics persisted to `ccmodel76ccb2_metrics` and available via `ML.EVALUATE`:
[agent]    - held-out **ROC AUC = 1.0**, precision 0.970, recall 0.980, F1 0.975, log-loss 0.0069.
[agent] 4. **Scoring → `ccpred76ccb2`** — `ML.PREDICT` over all 5,277 score rows. Schema: record key `transaction_id` + `fraud_probability`. Verified: 5,277 unique IDs, all probabilities in [0,1], no nulls, spread 0.0013–0.997.
[agent] ### Online/offline availability — partial, interface-limited
[agent] `ccpred76ccb2` is the offline feature table and is **clustered by `transaction_id`** so equality lookups on the record key prune to the relevant blocks — the BigQuery-native low-latency point-lookup path.
[agent] I could **not** stand up a dedicated managed **Vertex AI Feature Online Store** (the explicit online/offline-distinct serving layer): stable `gcloud ai` in this environment exposes no `feature-online-stores` / `feature-groups` / `feature-views` groups (only custom-jobs, endpoints, indexes, models, etc.), and `gcloud beta`/`gcloud alpha` are hard-blocked by the allowlist. So the managed online-store capability is **not reachable through the interface under test** — the BigQuery clustered table is the read path I could provide within it.
[agent] Everything else (feature group, training dataset, registered model with metrics, and the in-[0,1] prediction table for every score row) is complete on the platform, and the held-out ROC AUC clears the ≥ 0.749 target with strong margin on the internal split.
